## Hosting Platform Constraints

### GitHub Pages (FREE -- best for static project sites)

**Limits:**
- Site size: max 1 GB published
- Source repo: recommended max 1 GB
- Bandwidth: soft limit 100 GB/month (GitHub contacts you if exceeded; not hard-enforced)
- Builds: 10 per hour soft limit (does not apply if using GitHub Actions)
- Deployments: timeout at 10 minutes

**What you CAN do:**
- Static HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript
- Single-page applications (client-side JS routing)
- Custom domains with HTTPS (free, automatic via Let's Encrypt)
- Jekyll static site generator (built in) or any other SSG via Actions
- Prism.js or similar lightweight JS for syntax highlighting
- Images, favicons, Open Graph metadata
- Multiple pages, anchor navigation, responsive layouts

**What you CANNOT do:**
- Server-side code (no PHP, no Node.js backend, no databases)
- Form submissions (use a third-party like Formspree or Netlify Forms)
- E-commerce or SaaS (Terms of Service restriction)
- Server-side URL rewriting (SPAs need hash routing or 404.html trick)
- Sensitive transactions (passwords, credit cards)

**One custom domain per repo.** Each GitHub Pages site needs its own repo.

**Best for:** uniworld.world (project landing page, static, lives in its own repo already).

### GoDaddy Domain Forwarding (FREE with domain registration)

**What it does:** Redirects visitors from your domain to any other URL.
No hosting, no storage, no site -- just a redirect.

**Forwarding types (all free):**
- 301 Permanent redirect (default; best for SEO)
- 302 Temporary redirect
- Forwarding with masking (keeps your domain in address bar; not all destinations support this)

**HTTPS:** Automatically applied to forwarding.

**Best for:**
- worldof.world -> a GitHub Pages site OR a simple landing on Hostinger
- haimu.world -> aguywithai.world/haimu (if HAIMU content lives on the A Guy With AI site)
- Any domain that is a "landing redirect" to content hosted elsewhere

**Limitation:** No hosting. If you want even a single page at the domain, you need
either GitHub Pages, GoDaddy hosting, or Hostinger. Forwarding only redirects; it
does not serve files.

### GoDaddy Hosting (PAID -- Economy tier ~$6/month or ~$72/year)

**Economy plan includes:**
- 1 website, 25 GB storage, unmetered bandwidth
- Free domain with annual plan
- Free email (1 year)
- 99.99% uptime, DDoS protection

**When to use:** Only if you need a dedicated GoDaddy-hosted site for a domain that
cannot use GitHub Pages or Hostinger. For the current plan, this is NOT needed.

### Hostinger (ALREADY OWNED -- good limits)

**What you have:** Existing Hostinger account with aguywithai.world.

**Capabilities:**
- Multiple domains per account (can add worldof.world, haimu.world as addon domains)
- Subfolders as subdirectory sites (aguywithai.world/haimu, aguywithai.world/uniworld)
- Git auto-deploy from connected repo
- PHP, MySQL if needed (not needed for these sites)
- SSL, email, etc.

**Best for:** aguywithai.world (primary site with subpages for projects and methodology).
Can also host worldof.world and haimu.world as addon domains if GoDaddy forwarding
feels too limited.

