## Routing Architecture: Landing Pages and Content Hosting

### The Pattern: Landing Domain -> Content on Hostinger or GitHub Pages

For projects that grow, use the landing-page-to-content pattern:

```
uniworld.world  (GitHub Pages)   -- full standalone project site
haimu.world     (GoDaddy 301)    -> aguywithai.world/haimu  (Hostinger)
worldof.world   (GoDaddy 301 or GH Pages) -- simple link hub
aguywithai.world (Hostinger)     -- podcast + projects + methodology subpages
```

This pattern is **reusable for future projects**: each project gets a .world domain
that either hosts its own GitHub Pages site (if it has a dedicated repo) or forwards
to an aguywithai.world/projectname subpage.

### Business Subsidiary Pattern

```
grandbeta.world                  -- business landing
grandbeta.world/subsidiaryname   -- subsidiary page (or its own domain)
```

Managed separately in a business repo. Same pattern applies: landing domains can
forward to subpages.

